{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.root_of_unity_truncation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.root_of_unity_truncation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.root_of_unity_truncation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.root_of_unity_truncation","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/root_of_unity_truncation.lean#L56-L78","doc":"**Content statement** (from manuscript):\n\nThe [QOU axiom](#def:substrate-parameter) requires that $q$ is\n**not** a root of unity.  But the limit $q \\to 1$ passes through\na dense set of roots of unity, and at each root the\nrepresentation theory undergoes a dramatic truncation that\n**strengthens** regularity.  The blowup at $q = 1$ is the\naccumulation of infinitely many such truncations.\n\n    The Lean encoding below states the claim over the context class and\n    discharges it from the class's `impl_*` fields (§3b-conditional;\n    fully proved). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.impl_blowup_iff_levi_iff_kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.impl_blowup_iff_levi_iff_kappa","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/root_of_unity_truncation.lean#L54-L54","doc":"(v) Blowup iff Levi ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.impl_bernstein_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.impl_bernstein_bound","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/root_of_unity_truncation.lean#L52-L52","doc":"(iv) Bernstein bound at root of unity ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.impl_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.impl_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/root_of_unity_truncation.lean#L50-L50","doc":"(iii) Classical limit ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.impl_root_unity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.impl_root_unity","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/root_of_unity_truncation.lean#L48-L48","doc":"(ii) Root-of-unity truncation level `κ ≥ 2` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.impl_generic_qou_regime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.impl_generic_qou_regime","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/root_of_unity_truncation.lean#L46-L46","doc":"(i) Generic `q > 1` (QOU regime) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.truncation_active","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.truncation_active","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/root_of_unity_truncation.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Hypothesis that root of unity truncation is active. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.root_unity_truncated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.root_unity_truncated","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/root_of_unity_truncation.lean#L42-L42","doc":"Proposition: root of unity truncation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.leviNonDeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.leviNonDeg","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/root_of_unity_truncation.lean#L40-L40","doc":"Statement that the Levi form (contact form of the brane) stays\nnon-degenerate at the collision point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.nsBlowsUp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.nsBlowsUp","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/root_of_unity_truncation.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Statement that the Navier-Stokes system blows up at the\ncollision of two vortex filaments. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RootOfUnityTruncationContext.C","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/root_of_unity_truncation.lean#L34-L34","doc":"Universal Bernstein constant `C` for the trigonometric-polynomial\nbound `sup_t κ(t) ≤ 1 + C·(κ − 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},